From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Make the LuneOS plugin the default position source

QGeoPositionInfoSource::createDefaultSource() picks the position plugin
with the highest "Priority". This plugin and geoclue2 both declare 1000,
and Qt orders a tie by its QMultiHash of plugins, so which of the two a
process gets changes from one start to the next. On LuneOS geoclue2
gives nothing: its agent whitelist names no LuneOS component and its
modem sources expect ModemManager, not oFono. com.webos.service.location
is the location service the platform ships.

Declare priority 2000 so a default source on LuneOS is this plugin.
Clients that ask for a plugin by name are unaffected.

Seen with voicecall-manager's cell broadcast geofence on the mindphone:
of two restarts in a row, one created the LuneOS source and one the
geoclue2 source.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/plugin.json | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/plugin.json b/src/plugin.json
index badcc25..fffceff 100644
--- a/src/plugin.json
+++ b/src/plugin.json
@@ -4,5 +4,5 @@
     "Position": true,
     "Satellite": false,
     "Monitor" : false,
-    "Priority": 1000
+    "Priority": 2000
 }
